---
import "../styles.css";
import Analytics from "../components/Analytics.astro";
import { buttonVariants } from "../../../../src/client/components/ui/button";

const description = "A free, open-source media player everyone shares. Phones and laptops join with a QR code to choose what plays, play it, or share their own screen and sound.";
const repo = "https://github.com/avoid-quest/couch";
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" class="dark">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>About Couch</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:title" content="About Couch" />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={new URL("/about", Astro.site)} />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" />
    <Analytics />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <nav aria-label="Home"><a href="/"><img src="/mark.svg" width="24" height="24" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />couch.avoid.quest</a></nav>
      <h1>A media player everyone shares.</h1>
      <p class="intro">Run Couch on the computer by the TV. Everyone else scans a QR code with their phone or laptop, no app or account, and joins in: pick what plays next, hear it on their own device too, or put their own screen on the TV.</p>
      <p><a class={buttonVariants()} href="/download">Download the preview</a></p>

      <section>
        <h2>Choose together</h2>
        <p>Search YouTube, Twitch, Bandcamp, radio, Live TV and film, series and anime catalogues, or paste a link, from your own phone. It all goes into one Up next that everyone shares, and anyone can play, pause or skip.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Play it where you want</h2>
        <p>The TV takes the picture, the kitchen laptop takes the sound, and they play in step. A phone or laptop that joins can lend its screen or speakers too, once its owner allows it.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Share what you're playing</h2>
        <p>Playing a game on your laptop? Share its screen and sound to the TV and your friends' laptops. Each one plays it the moment it arrives, so the delay stays small when the network lets them connect directly.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Get started</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Download Couch for Mac, Windows or Linux, open it on the computer that will play, and choose <strong>Host on this computer</strong>.</li>
          <li>Name it and share it on your network. Couch shows a QR code.</li>
          <li>Scan the code with your phone. Because Couch lives on your network rather than the internet, the browser warns once that the connection isn't private; continue, name your phone, and you're in. Friends join the same way.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Couch is free and open source, and in preview: it updates itself, and it changes quickly.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Live sound <span class="soon">Coming soon</span></h2>
        <p>Plug a mixer into the Couch computer. Everyone at the gig joins the Wi-Fi, scans a code and listens on their own phone or headphones: close to live, in step with the phones around them, in good stereo, for the whole set.</p>
        <p>Part of this works today: Couch can send a sound card's input to other devices. But you have to choose between fast, with each phone on its own timing, and in step, a few seconds behind the stage. Live sound means both at once. It's in the lab, not in a release yet. <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/product/vision.md`}>Read the plan</a></p>
      </section>

      <footer>
        <a href="/download">Download</a>
        <a href={repo}>GitHub</a>
        <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/usage.md#what-plays-where`}>What plays where</a>
        <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/live-inputs.md`}>How sharing works</a>
        <a href="https://avoid.quest">A project of avoid.quest</a>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  main { max-width: 48rem; margin: auto; padding: 2rem var(--gutter) 4rem; }
  nav a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .5rem; font-size: .875rem; color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  nav a:hover, footer a:hover { color: var(--foreground); }
  h1 { margin: 3rem 0 .5rem; font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; line-height: 2rem; letter-spacing: -.012em; }
  h2 { font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .soon { margin-left: .5rem; font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: .875rem; font-weight: 400; color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  section { margin-top: 3rem; }
  p, ol { margin-top: .75rem; max-width: 60ch; font-size: .875rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .intro { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  ol { padding-left: 1.25rem; list-style: decimal; }
  ol li + li { margin-top: .5rem; }
  strong { font-weight: 500; color: var(--foreground); }
  p a:not([class]) { color: var(--foreground); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: .2em; }
  footer { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .5rem 1.5rem; margin-top: 4rem; font-size: .75rem; color: var(--muted-foreground); }
</style>
